preamble
name "Full-duplex tiny-buffer torture"
description "Bidirectional marked streams cross while both TCP windows are constrained"
owner "network-team"
timeout 30s
begin using tcp
server at local
client at local
server listen "127.0.0.1:49292"
client connect "127.0.0.1:49292"
server set-sndbuf 4KiB
server set-rcvbuf 4KiB
client set-sndbuf 4KiB
client set-rcvbuf 4KiB
# Jobs start immediately and run independently on both agents.
server drain 2MiB stamp-every 4KiB
client drain 2MiB stamp-every 4096B
server transmit 2MiB stamp-every 4096B chunk 113B delay 1ms
client transmit 2MiB stamp-every 4KiB chunk 127B delay 1ms
server await-tx
client await-tx
server half-close-write
client half-close-write
server await-rx
client await-rx
server receive-eot
client receive-eot
server close
client close
end
outcome pass
when server.rx.bytes == 2MiB
and server.rx.integrity == valid
and client.rx.bytes == 2MiB
and client.rx.integrity == valid
describe "Both stamped streams and crossed FINs passed without loss or corruption."
outcome fail "The proxy corrupted or truncated the full-duplex stream."
outcome timeout "The proxy stalled during concurrent full-duplex traffic, with small buffers, or with crossed FINs."
end
